s2n-bignum x86 decoder: Do not rely on physical sharing of terms

Scope: the s2n-bignum copy used for recording only.

DECODE_LEN_THM walks an x86 byte list until it reaches, by physical
equality (`==`), the tail that DECODE_CONV returned; two similar
walkers in the same file do likewise. While HOLTrace records, its
kernel wrappers replace objects with structurally equal copies from
the trace tables, so the tail is equal but not shared, the walk runs
past it, and the proof fails with Failure "DECODE_LEN_THM". Without
HOLTrace the same build succeeds.

Also accept a structurally equal tail (`compare ... = 0`). The tails
of a list have different lengths, so this matches the same tail as
before.

Trusted-base impact: the patched decoder is outside the trusted base.
The replay build loads neither s2n-bignum nor this patch. It
reconstructs every accepted theorem through its own kernel.

--- a/x86/proofs/decode.ml
+++ b/x86/proofs/decode.ml
@@ -2962,13 +2962,13 @@
